EXTENSION "ARMDef_Tales_of_Mythic_Europe_WhatLiesBeneath_TobiasMahlNewMasterOfTheWorks" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Tales of Mythic Europe - Tobias Mahl, New Master of the Works"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-09"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Tales_of_Mythic_Europe_Core_Ext"

    # Tobias Mahl, New Master of the Works (Chapter Ten: What Lies Beneath, p157): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #tccde5ec02fc6b9b8c34fec ^"Tobias Mahl, New Master of the Works" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Characteristics" STRING "Int +1, Per 0, Pre +2, Com +1, Str 0, Sta +1, Dex +1, Qik 0"
            ^"Size" STRING "0"
            ^"Age" STRING "34 (34)"
            ^"Decrepitude" STRING "0"
            ^"Warping Score" STRING "2 (15)"
            ^"Confidence Score" STRING "1 (3)"
            ^"Virtues and Flaws" STRING "Priest; Summoner, Summoning, Commanding; Educated, Student of Infernal, Strong-Willed; Dark Secret (diabolist), Corrupted Abilities (Engineer), Avaricious, Vow (Celibacy)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Affable +2, Confident +1, Avaricious +2"
            ^"Reputations" STRING "Fine Engineer +3 (Flanders), Fine Engineer +1 (Northern Europe), Avaricious +2 (Infernal)"
            ^"Hierarchy" STRING "2"
            ^"Combat" STRING "Dodge: Init +0, Attack N/A, Defense +0, Damage N/A Fist: Init +0, Attack +1, Defense +0, Damage –1 Knife: Init +0, Attack +2, Defense +0, Damage +2"
            ^"Soak" STRING "+1"
            ^"Fatigue Levels" STRING "OK, 0, –1, –3, –5, Unconscious"
            ^"Wound Penalties" STRING "–1 (1–5), –3 (6–10), –5 (11–15), Incapacitated (16–20), Dead (21+)"
            ^"Abilities" STRING "Area Lore: Romney Marsh 1 (geography), Area Lore: Flanders 3 (Bruges), Artes Liberales 1 (arithmetic), Charm 2 (first impressions), Church Lore 2 (engineering works), Civil and Canon Law 1 (Lex Marisci), Concentration 3 (summoning), Engineer 4 (marsh inning), Etiquette 2 (the church), Flemish 5 (Bruges), Folk Ken 3 (clergy), French 3 (laborers), Infernal Lore 4 (demons), Intrigue 3 (plotting), Latin 4 (academic usage), Leadership 2 (inspiration), Penetration 2 (summoning), Philosophiae 1 (metaphysics), Teaching 2 (Summoning), Theology 3 (heresy)"
            ^"Goetic Arts" STRING "Commanding 9, Summoning 10"
            ^"Equipment" STRING "Fine clothes and various note books on past engineering works."
            ^"Encumbrance" STRING "0 (0)"
            ^"Appearance" STRING "A good-looking man who carries himself with confidence. He has fair hair that he does not tonsure. Since arriving at Battle, he has taken to wearing robes of black velvet; clearly expensive but respectfully close to the garb of his Benedictine hosts."
            ^"Source" STRING "Tales of Mythic Europe"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 157
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Born in Bruges, Tobias learned his letters and was ordained at the cathedral school at Noyon. But he was intent on the worldly life of money and soon returned to Bruges to work the marshes and learn his trade as an engineer.\n\nIt was then that the demon Mammon sent one of his many minions to take human form and make himself a rival to Tobias. The rival belittled and humiliated Tobias at every turn. But soon, despairing at ever beating his mortal enemy, Tobias was happy to be ruled by his pride and he accepted Mammon’s dark guidance. Of course, with the pact made and his rival bested, Tobias’ name once more began to spread and his coffers swelled.\n\nTobias has been in the grip of the Infernal for the last seven years. In that time, Tobias has studied the Goetic Arts, becoming a summoner of Infernal spirits.\n\nTobias Mahl is calculatingly affable and confident, and makes for easy company. He is practical and pragmatic and exudes reliability. But he uses corrupt blessings (mixing urine with the communion wine or holy water) and his personal influence to slowly corrupt the laborers working in the marsh. Over time, they develop an Arrogant +1 personality trait."
    }

}
